  "type": "numeric",
  "prompt": "Compute\n$$\\lim_{n\\to1}\\sum_{k=1}^{25}\\frac{n^k-1}{\\ln(n)}.$$",
  "image": null,
  "choices": null,
  "answer": "325",
  "acceptedAnswers": null,
  "answerUnit": null,
  "solutions": [
   {
    "title": "Termwise limits",
    "body": "Each term is a derivative: $\\lim_{n\\to1}\\frac{n^k-1}{\\ln n}=\\lim\\frac{kn^{k-1}}{1/n}=k$ (L'Hopital). The sum is finite, so the limit is $1+2+\\cdots+25=\\frac{25\\cdot26}{2}=325$.\n\n**Answer: 325**"
   }
  ],
