  "type": "numeric",
  "prompt": "Compute\n$$\\int_0^\\pi\\sin^{10}(x)\\,dx.$$",
  "image": null,
  "choices": null,
  "answer": "63*pi/256",
  "answerDisplay": "$\\frac{63\\pi}{256}$",
  "acceptedAnswers": null,
  "answerUnit": null,
  "solutions": [
   {
    "title": "Reduction formula",
    "body": "Integration by parts gives $\\int_0^\\pi\\sin^nx\\,dx=\\frac{n-1}{n}\\int_0^\\pi\\sin^{n-2}x\\,dx$. With $\\int_0^\\pi 1\\,dx=\\pi$: $\\int_0^\\pi\\sin^{10}x\\,dx=\\pi\\cdot\\frac12\\cdot\\frac34\\cdot\\frac56\\cdot\\frac78\\cdot\\frac9{10}=\\frac{63\\pi}{256}$.\n\n**Answer: $\\frac{63\\pi}{256}$**"
   },
   {
    "title": "Expand",
    "body": "$\\sin^{10}x=\\frac1{2^{10}}\\binom{10}{5}+(\\text{terms in }\\cos(2jx),\\ j\\ge1)$, and the cosine terms integrate to $0$ over $[0,\\pi]$. So the integral is $\\pi\\binom{10}{5}/1024=\\frac{252\\pi}{1024}=\\frac{63\\pi}{256}$.\n\n**Answer: $\\frac{63\\pi}{256}$**"
   }
  ],
